<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50685" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vescus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		contr. from veesca. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Small</i>, <i>little</i>, <i>thin</i>, <i>weak</i>, <i>feeble</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">farra (opp. vegrandia),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					3, 445</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">papaver,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 4, 131</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frondes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 175</span></i>
			 Serv.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corpus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 20, 19, § 81</span></i>
			: vires, Afran. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. p. 187,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Poor</i>, <i>wretched</i>:
			fastidiosum ac vescum vivere, Lucil. ap. <i><span class="en">Non.
				p. 186, 32</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>corroding</i>, <i>eating away</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sal,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					1, 326</span></i>
			 Munro ad loc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
